{"title":"Career Roadmap · ECMO Specialist","role":"ECMO Specialist","summary":"An ECMO Specialist is an advanced critical-care allied-health professional who supports the management of patients receiving extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO). ECMO temporarily supports heart and/or lung function by circulating blood through an extracorporeal circuit for gas exchange and, depending on configuration, circulatory support.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Perfusion Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An ECMO Specialist is an advanced critical-care allied-health professional who supports the management of patients receiving extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO). ECMO temporarily supports heart and/or lung function by circulating blood through an extracorporeal circuit for gas exchange and, depending on configuration, circulatory support."},{"type":"p","text":"The role requires strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiopulmonary physiology"},{"text":"Perfusion technology"},{"text":"ECMO circuits"},{"text":"Blood pumps"},{"text":"Oxygenators"},{"text":"Hemodynamic monitoring"},{"text":"Ventilation concepts"},{"text":"Anticoagulation awareness"},{"text":"Critical-care medicine"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Circuit troubleshooting"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important pathway consideration"},{"type":"p","text":"ECMO Specialist is generally not a direct-entry role immediately after a bachelor's degree. A realistic pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Perfusion Technology Degree","Clinical Perfusion / Cardiopulmonary Experience","Critical-Care & ECMO Training","Supervised ECMO Practice","ECMO Specialist","Senior ECMO Specialist","ECMO Coordinator / Lead","ECMO Program / Critical-Care Operations"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact cr